    "text": "Level Process Trainer (ACE 101) 58 7. About Us 7.1 Introduction With a strong focus on applied learning, Advanced Control Equipments develops miniaturized industrial working models for laboratory environments. We design and manufacture laboratory modules that provide hands-on training across disciplines including mechanical, electrical, electronics, mechatronics, instrumentation, and chemical engineering. With over two decades of experience, ACE is committed to delivering industry -standard equipment at affordable prices. Our product range includes process control systems, instrumentation systems, mechatronics setups, PLC and microcontroller-based systems, home automation solutions, and more. Using our powerful in -house software, we support both real -time control and model -based simulation and control. Our user -friendly simulation / hardware interface tools help aspiring engine ers understand key concepts such as mathematical mode lling, controller design and analysis, PID tuning, and model -based control strategies. We also enable users to implement custom control algorithms, in addition to built -in advanced control techniques such as Fuzzy Control, Gain Scheduling, and Model Predictive Control. 7.2 Vision and Values Vision To develop industry-standard laboratory products in the field of instrumentation and process control, enabling effective and meaningful teaching–learning experiences. Values • Over two decades of experience in laboratory equipment design and development • Capability to deliver solutions for a wide range of instrumentation and process control applications • User-friendly hardware - software interfaces • Customizable product designs based on customer requirements • Commitment to timely delivery as promised 7.3 Product Range From fundamental concepts to advanced model-based control, Advanced Control Equipments offers a wide range of equipment and tools. With strong expertise in both hardware and software, ACE supports faculty, students, and the research community in areas such as process control, mode lling and simulation, instrumentation systems, chemical and m echanical systems, data acquisition, and the Internet of Things. Based on the application, the products are grouped as given below:"
